  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Add a primary world's list to VRChat to help push users to visit these worlds\nCurrently we have \"most activity\" and dev choice at the top of the worlds list but this is heavily reliant on user flow and traffic. This means that users would most likely go to places with the most activity, these new worlds that can't gain initial traction of having 100+ users in it at a once would likely never be visited\n\nPushing players to visit these worlds by adding a \"Flavor channel\" will help creators get their product to the world simply by having this ontop of the list\n\nFor those people who claim that this will do nothing to improve world variety, let us give a coming example to help prove this point\n\nWithin a few short weeks, we will have Virtual Market, an event where the Overseas VRC community puts their creations on display for visitors to come and experience\n\nI will lobby for first test of this system is to have \"Virtual Market\" worlds as the \"flavor of the week/Event\" world list for the duration of the event in an effort to help bolster user activity.\n\nThe goal of the \"Flavor of the Week/Event\" world list is to bring much needed user activity to these worlds that would otherwise be burried below top activity worlds, Like \"the Box\" or \"the Room in Rain\"",
